<svg viewBox="0 0 720 420" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Inference performance metrics">
  <!-- latency timeline -->
  <text x="40" y="30" font-size="13.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Anatomy of latency (streaming)</text>

  <rect x="40" y="44" width="170" height="46" rx="8" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)" />
  <text x="125" y="63" font-size="11.5" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--accent-ink)">TTFT</text>
  <text x="125" y="80" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">time to first token = prefill</text>

  <rect x="214" y="44" width="466" height="46" rx="8" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="447" y="63" font-size="11.5" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)">TPOT × number of output tokens</text>
  <text x="447" y="80" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">time per output token = decode · ~120 ms/token ≈ reading speed is enough</text>

  <text x="40" y="116" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">total latency = TTFT + TPOT × tokens · same total can feel different — instant first token vs faster stream is a UX choice</text>
  <text x="40" y="134" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">user-visible TTFT ≠ model TTFT when hidden steps run (CoT, agent plans) — some teams track “time to publish”</text>
  <text x="40" y="152" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">latency is a distribution: report p50/p90/p99, never the average — one 3s outlier poisons the mean</text>

  <!-- throughput -->
  <rect x="40" y="174" width="310" height="106" rx="10" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="60" y="200" font-size="12.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Throughput → cost</text>
  <text x="60" y="220" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">output tokens/s across all users (also RPM)</text>
  <text x="60" y="238" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">$2/h compute ÷ 100 tokens/s ≈ $5.56 / 1M tokens</text>
  <text x="60" y="256" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">trade-off: batching can 2–3× throughput</text>
  <text x="60" y="272" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">at the price of TTFT/TPOT</text>

  <!-- goodput -->
  <rect x="370" y="174" width="310" height="106" rx="10" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="390" y="200" font-size="12.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Goodput — throughput that counts</text>
  <text x="390" y="220" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">requests/s that MEET your SLO</text>
  <text x="390" y="238" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">(e.g. TTFT ≤ 200ms, TPOT ≤ 100ms)</text>
  <text x="390" y="256" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">100 completed but only 30 within SLO</text>
  <text x="390" y="272" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">→ goodput = 30 — optimize THIS, not raw RPS</text>

  <!-- utilization -->
  <rect x="40" y="296" width="640" height="100" rx="10" fill="var(--bg-raised)" stroke="var(--line)" />
  <text x="58" y="320" font-size="12.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Utilization — but the right kind</text>
  <text x="58" y="340" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">nvidia-smi “GPU utilization” = % of time busy — a chip doing 1 of its 100 possible ops/s still reports 100%. Nearly useless.</text>
  <text x="58" y="358" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">MFU = achieved tokens/s ÷ theoretical peak FLOP/s throughput (training &gt;50% is good; inference lower, prefill &gt; decode)</text>
  <text x="58" y="376" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">MBU = (params × bytes/param × tokens/s) ÷ peak bandwidth — e.g. 7B × 2 bytes × 100 tok/s = 1.4 TB/s ÷ 2 TB/s = 70%</text>
</svg>
